From 89c722c9a0fd91ccfe2b60b24b76b1a4cddc8269 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branch <andrewbranch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:53:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Accept compact project handles in API requests

Every checker request repeated the project's full ID (its config file path).
Project responses now include a short handle ("#N"), assigned from a
process-wide table, that the client sends instead; request decoding maps
handles back to project IDs. Full project IDs are still accepted.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
